// FIXED — the forward-edge ordering hole (2026-08-20 audit,
// design/activation_state.md; found via the dyncall_seed_backedge
// fixture regressing under the loud-degrade Err). Kernel definition
// order was REVERSED DECLARATION ORDER as a callees-first
// approximation, which breaks on SIBLING discovery: the root
// references g before f (the shielding select's arm), so discovery
// records [g, f], the reversal defined f FIRST, f's g-call found no
// SiteLayout, and the old silent-0 fallback ran g's activations
// below f's recursion with NO interior memory — g's guard ride cache
// never stored, so when m goes bottom (epochs 3-4) the sound
// scrutinee re-match found no history and bottomed where the
// interp's retained instance rode its held selection:
//   interp: [101, 1, 1, 1]   jit (pre-fix): [101, 1]
// Fixed by TOPOLOGICAL definition order over the recorded static
// call edges (emit/jit.rs) — the only layout legitimately missing at
// a caller's definition is now its OWN (self-calls, resolved through
// the site_desc cell), and emit_site_block Errs loudly if the
// invariant breaks instead of passing 0. f must be NON-tail here
// (`+ i64:0`): the tail twin's frames clear the ride per pass on the
// interp too (the mid-loop residue, a separate chapter).
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:0, i64:0]); let m = x / x / i64:3; let g = |k: i64| -> i64 select k - k {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => i64:1, _ => i64:2}; let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => g(n), _ => f(n - i64:1) + i64:0}; select x {i64:1 => g(i64:5), _ => i64:0} * i64:100 + f(x - x + i64:1)}
